From: Rick Carback <rick.carback@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rtc: qcom-glink: Fail a set-property the firmware refuses

The SET_PROPERTY response carries the firmware status in its property
word. The driver ignored it, so an alarm the firmware refuses (the QN10
answers ALARM_ENABLE=1 with 0x202) was reported as armed and rtcwake
waited for an alarm that never came. Return -EIO instead.
---
diff --git a/drivers/rtc/rtc-qcom-glink.c b/drivers/rtc/rtc-qcom-glink.c
index 61baf5f..f664c91 100644
--- a/drivers/rtc/rtc-qcom-glink.c
+++ b/drivers/rtc/rtc-qcom-glink.c
@@ -145,6 +145,16 @@ static int qcom_rtc_glink_set_property(struct qcom_rtc_glink *rtc_glink,
 		RTC_GLINK_SET_PROPERTY, property, value);
 	mutex_lock(&rtc_glink->lock);
 	ret = qcom_rtc_glink_request(rtc_glink, &msg, sizeof(msg));
+	/*
+	 * The SET_PROPERTY response carries the firmware status in the
+	 * property word; anything other than 0 means the write was refused
+	 * (the QN10 firmware answers ALARM_ENABLE=1 with 0x202).
+	 */
+	if (!ret && rtc_glink->resp_valid && rtc_glink->resp_value) {
+		dev_dbg(rtc_glink->dev, "property %u refused: status 0x%x\n",
+			property, rtc_glink->resp_value);
+		ret = -EIO;
+	}
 	mutex_unlock(&rtc_glink->lock);
 	return ret;
 }
